From d89648c49aee6c6067cf5e051be8f62af747591d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Boris=20Sta=CC=88heli?= <ich@bstaehe.li>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:03:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add configurable user button actions

Add UserButtonActions, an opt-in mapping from user button gestures to
actions for devices without a screen: send an alert text (optionally
followed by an ad-hoc position), acknowledge a running external
notification nag with a reply text, send a position, or do nothing.

Settings are read through UserButtonActionsConfig, whose fields mirror a
possible future module config message. For now it is filled from build
flags (UBA_*) with neutral English defaults. Alerts are rate-limited by
alert_min_interval_secs.

Everything outside the hardware-free decision logic is compiled only with
MESHTASTIC_USER_BUTTON_ACTIONS (default off). The decision logic is
covered by native unit tests in test/test_user_button_actions.
